[5]
task: explicit-alignment::frontend_sema
status: done
desc: Parse alignment arguments and recognized companion attributes, then validate all declaration sites and values.
impl:
  - Extend /home/diogo/Zith/src/frontend/frontend.hpp Attribute with an optional expression id for attribute arguments and AttributeKind values for AlignAs, NoAlias, Likely, and Unlikely.
  - Update AstLowerer::parseAttributes in /home/diogo/Zith/src/frontend/ast-lowerer.cpp to parse parenthesized attribute expressions while preserving the full span.
  - Update /home/diogo/Zith/src/frontend/attribute-classify.hpp so alignas is limited to ordinary structs and permitted bindings, noalias to functions, and likely/unlikely are recognized names.
  - Validate alignas duplicates and unsupported fields, parameters, components, unions, and enums with errors rather than warnings.
  - In sema, require alignas to evaluate to a positive power-of-two integer constant independent of generic parameters and reject target-unsupported values.
  - Require noalias functions to return a pointer; do not add optimizer or branch-likelihood behavior for these parser attributes.
  - Preserve accepted module-scope const bindings without introducing new global declaration forms.
tests:
  | id | dado | quando | então |
  | F-1 | #[alignas(N)] attribute syntax | frontend parses a struct or binding | one argument expression and its source span are retained |
  | F-2 | unsupported placement or invalid N | TypeChecked runs | compilation fails with an error diagnostic |
  | F-3 | companion attribute | noalias targets a non-pointer return | compilation fails with an error diagnostic |
  | F-4 | likely/unlikely attributes | frontend parses a declaration | neither spelling is diagnosed as unknown |

