task: explicit-alignment::type_layout
status: done
desc: Carry struct alignment through canonical types and compute padded field offsets, size, and array stride consistently.
impl:
  - Add requested struct alignment to /home/diogo/Zith/src/sema/modern-types.hpp and every ordinary and generic struct construction path.
  - Carry the effective alignment into /home/diogo/Zith/src/types/type-intern.hpp StructDef and its definition helpers.
  - Update /home/diogo/Zith/src/types/type-canonical.cpp so field offsets use aligned offsets, aggregate size is tail-padded to aggregate alignment, and array size uses aligned element stride.
  - Include explicit alignment in canonical type identity and preserve foreign C layout behavior.
  - Update /home/diogo/Zith/src/codegen/codegen-type.cpp with an LLVM representation that preserves field indexes while matching the promised explicit alignment and padded size.
  - Confirm target support against the configured LLVM DataLayout and return a semantic diagnostic rather than emitting unsupported layouts.
tests:
  | id | dado | quando | então |
  | L-1 | ABI-ALIGN-01 fixture | layout tests compile on x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu | offsets are 0 and 0/64 as specified; sizes and alignments are 64, 128, and 64 |
  | L-2 | aligned struct array | layout is queried | element stride is 64 and [2] size is 128 |
  | L-3 | canonical identity | otherwise-identical struct definitions request different alignments | their canonical identities differ |

