task: explicit-alignment::binding_storage
status: done
desc: Propagate binding-only alignment through HIR to native and VM storage allocation.
impl:
  - Add alignment bytes to /home/diogo/Zith/src/hir/hir-attrs.hpp HirSlotAttrs and module-scope HirGlobalConst metadata.
  - In /home/diogo/Zith/src/sema/hir-lower-stmt.cpp, attach validated alignment to each annotated local binding slot.
  - In /home/diogo/Zith/src/sema/hir-lower-modern.cpp, attach alignment to permitted module-scope const storage.
  - Apply the requested LLVM alignment to allocas in /home/diogo/Zith/src/codegen/codegen-emit-expr.cpp and globals in the global emission path.
  - Use per-slot alignment in /home/diogo/Zith/src/vm/hir-to-vm.cpp rather than the fixed alignment immediate.
  - Keep the declared type and array element stride unchanged for binding-level alignment.
tests:
  | id | dado | quando | então |
  | B-1 | #[alignas(64)] local [128]u8 | native codegen runs | base storage is 64-byte aligned while type size remains 128 |
  | B-2 | copy from aligned binding to ordinary binding | both bindings are emitted | only the annotated destination receives the stronger alignment |
  | B-3 | aligned local in VM | VM runs the test fixture | the slot address satisfies the requested alignment |

