task: explicit-alignment::runtime_and_cache
status: done
desc: Persist aligned type and storage metadata and enforce safe C ABI boundaries across supported execution paths.
impl:
  - Extend compact struct definitions and HIR slot/global records in /home/diogo/Zith/src/cache/cache-types.hpp and /home/diogo/Zith/src/cache/artifact-builder.cpp.
  - Encode and decode the new metadata in /home/diogo/Zith/src/zirl/zirl-type-section.cpp, /home/diogo/Zith/src/zirl/zirl-attrs-section.cpp, and /home/diogo/Zith/src/session/persistent-cache.cpp.
  - Bump only the necessary schema or container versions and preserve explicit compatibility rejection for old artifacts.
  - Reject aligned C by-value records unless foreign layout metadata proves the exact type layout and alignment; preserve existing unsupported-record diagnostics.
  - Verify HIR interpreter and VM allocation paths do not silently lose binding alignment guarantees.
tests:
  | id | dado | quando | então |
  | C-1 | aligned type and slot metadata | cache encode/decode round-trips | requested type and storage alignments are unchanged |
  | C-2 | aligned value at unverified C ABI boundary | semantic/codegen boundary is checked | a diagnostic prevents emission |
  | C-3 | old artifact schema | cache reader loads artifact | stale incompatible metadata is rejected or invalidated explicitly |

